{"tool_name":"vtools","contents":["biocontainers","oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biocontainers":{"name":"vtools","identifiers":["biotools:vtools","doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/btr667"],"license":"MIT","summary":"Various tools operating over VCF files. Uses cyvcf2 and cython under the hood for speed","home_url":"https://github.com/LUMC/vtools","keywords":["Genetic Variation","Genome, Human","High-Throughput Nucleotide Sequencing","Humans","Metabolic Networks and Pathways","Molecular Sequence Annotation","User-Computer Interface","Exome sequencing","Genotype and phenotype","Workflows"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":204},"biotools":{"id":"vtools","home":"http://varianttools.sourceforge.net/","summary":"Software for annotating and tracking sequence variation for large-scale exome sequencing projects.","addition_date":"2019-05-28T08:57:08Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-25T13:45:32.084525Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:vtools","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"bpeng@mdanderson.org","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"note":"Tutorial material","type":["Training material"],"url":"http://varianttools.sourceforge.net/Main/Documentation"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Genotyping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3196"},{"term":"Variant calling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3227"},{"term":"Variant filtering","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3675"}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"vtools","operating_system":["Linux","Mac"],"owner":"Ruta","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btr667","metadata":{"abstract":"Motivation: Storing, annotating and analyzing variants from next-generation sequencing projects can be difficult due to the availability of a wide array of data formats, tools and annotation sources, as well as the sheer size of the data files. Useful tools, including the GATK, ANNOVAR and BEDTools can be integrated into custom pipelines for annotating and analyzing sequence variants. However, building flexible pipelines that support the tracking of variants alongside their samples, while enabling updated annotation and reanalyses, is not a simple task.Results: We have developed variant tools, a flexible annotation and analysis toolset that greatly simplifies the storage, annotation and filtering of variants and the analysis of the underlying samples. variant tools can be used to manage and analyze genetic variants obtained from sequence alignments, and the command-line driven toolset could be used as a foundation for building more sophisticated analytical methods. \u00a9 The Author 2011. Published by Oxford University Press. All rights reserved.","authors":[{"name":"Peng B."},{"name":"San lucas F.A."},{"name":"Scheet P."},{"name":"Wang G."}],"citationCount":120,"date":"2012-02-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"Integrated annotation and analysis of genetic variants from next-generation sequencing studies with variant tools"},"pmcid":"PMC3268240","pmid":"22138362","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Exome sequencing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3676"},{"term":"Genotype and phenotype","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0625"},{"term":"Workflows","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0769"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"vtools","home":"https://bio.tools/vtools","summary":"Software for annotating and tracking sequence variation for large-scale exome sequencing projects.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:vtools/cmd/varianttools.sourceforge.net","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":null,"registration":null},"packages":null,"source_packages":false,"sourcecode":{"free":null,"interpreted":true,"license":null,"